  "hindi": "पुकारता हुआ, अपनी जाति की घोषणा करता हुआ वह अपनी वाणी को ऐसे छोड़ता है जैसे नाविक नाव को। हे पक्षी, तुम शुभ लक्षण वाले हो जाओ; कोई भी अभिभूत करने वाली, सर्वव्यापी शक्ति तुम्हें न पाए।",
  "english": "Crying out, proclaiming his kind, he sends forth his voice like an oarsman a boat. And be of good omen, O bird; may no overpowering, all-pervading one at all find you.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Obscure. januṣam is taken as \"birth, kind\"; aritā iva nāvam is read \"like an oarsman (drives) a boat\" with the verb carried over from iyarti. abhibhā and viśvyā are f. nom. sg. forms agreeing with kā, sense unclear (\"overpowering, all-pervading\"). The verse could also mean \"may no all-pervading overpowering (thing) find you\".",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
