  "hindi": "तुम्हें न बाज़ मार गिराए, न सुपर्ण, और न बाण वाला वीर धनुर्धर तुम्हें पाए। पितरों की दिशा के साथ-साथ पुकारते हुए, शुभ लक्षण वाले, कल्याणकारी वचन बोलने वाले, यहाँ बोलो।",
  "english": "Let not the hawk strike you down, nor the fair-winged bird; let not the hero with arrows, the archer, find you. Crying out along the direction of the fathers, of good omen, speaking what is good, speak here.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "ud vadhīt: the exact force of ud with √vadh is uncertain (\"strike up / strike down\"). suparṇa is \"fair-winged\" (a bird) and is not identified further. pitryām pradiśam rendered literally as \"the direction of the fathers\"; no interpretation of which quarter is meant is applied.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
