  "hindi": "घरों के दक्षिण की ओर से पुकारो, हे शुभ लक्षण वाले, कल्याणकारी वचन बोलने वाले पक्षी। न चोर हम पर अधिकार करे, न बुरी बात कहने वाला; हम उत्तम वीरों से युक्त होकर यज्ञ में महान् वचन बोलें।",
  "english": "Cry out from the right side of the houses, O bird of good omen, speaking what is good. Let neither a thief nor a speaker of evil have power over us; may we, rich in heroes, speak greatly in the rite.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dakṣiṇataḥ is \"from the right\" or \"from the south\"; the more literal \"right side\" is used. śakunte is taken as a feminine vocative (śakunti); it could be a masculine form of the same bird. na̭: in line 2 is naḥ (colon = visarga).",
